      "The anharmonicity, the difference between the first and second transition frequencies, which lets the qubit be addressed as a two-level system, also decreases with the ratio, but only as a power law, roughly as the inverse of the square root of the ratio. For ratios around 50, the charge dispersion is negligible compared with other sources of noise, and the anharmonicity remains a few percent of the qubit frequency, about 200 to 300 megahertz for a typical device, which is sufficient for fast gates.",
