    technicalAbstract: "A quantum computer can be implemented with cold ions confined in a linear trap and interacting with laser beams. Each ion represents a qubit, with the logical states being two internal levels. The collective quantized motion of the ions provides a bus for transferring quantum information, and a controlled-NOT gate is realized using laser pulses that couple the ions' internal states to the motion. The authors discuss the effect of decoherence and the experimental requirements.",
